Fillets: a contact that runs along a part of an edge of its face
(mitcad#121): e.g. a channel whose side wall is exactly as high as the
rounding at its foot and whose floor rounds down at the part's ends; along
the straight part the rounding's contact runs along the wall's top edge,
round the floor's end roundings it lies inside the wall, so the wall keeps
a piece at each end.

- ChFi3d_ContactsAlongFaceEdges (0014, 0017) took a contact on a face as
  running along an edge of the face only when it covered the whole edge
  (from vertex to vertex). It now also takes a contact that covers a part
  of an edge, one end or both at inner points of the edge
  (runsAlongEdgePart). The surface data is converted as before (the
  contact is on the face beyond, the edge is its curve); each inner end
  gets the edge as its arc, at the point's parameter, with the transition
  of a contact on the face leaving it across the edge (at the first end)
  or coming back (at the last), and so does the neighbouring surface data
  whose contact on the face comes to the edge there, so that the edge is
  cut there and its rest stays with the face's pieces. Where the neighbour
  runs along the same edge, the edge is not cut. Before, the contact stayed
  on the face, along its boundary, and the result's wire of the face
  intersected itself.
